WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:03.840
Utopianism.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.760
Utopianism is the ism of utopias.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.560
It means a belief or interest
in a perfect world -

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.040
or at least a world
designed to be perfect.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.240
The word 'utopia' was coined in 1516
by Sir Thomas More -

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.680
writer, saint and opponent
of Henry the VIII's marriage plans -

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.440
in his book of the same name.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.120
Utopia has been taken
by some people at face value

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.280
as a book about a perfect land.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.200
But others point to the fact that
the word 'utopia' literally means...

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.000
and that the book is a satire.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.560
But that hasn’t stopped people.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.840
Through the years
there has been all sorts of ideas

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.280
about a perfect society.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.480
Economic utopias with no poverty...

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.640
ecological utopias where humans
live in harmony with nature

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.440
and so on and so forth.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.800
Many cultures and religions

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.160
have a myth
of a perfect society in the past,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.760
like the Garden of Eden.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.200
Communes, music festivals
and naturist camps

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.200
could all be seen as attempts
to create a mini utopia on Earth.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.480
There are many kinds of utopias

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.760
but one of the central qualities
of any utopia, paradoxically,

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.240
is that it doesn’t exist.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:07.200
Being a utopianist
essentially means being a dreamer.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.400
When John Lennon sang,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.040
"You may say I'm a dreamer"

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.840
in his famous hit single
and utopian anthem, Imagine,

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.280
he was referring
to exactly this quality.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.480
Utopianism's main flaw
is its obsession with perfection.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.760
This can lead to absurdities
like the Soviet Russian belief

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.360
that one day all crime
would be eradicated

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.880
because under true socialism
crime would not be necessary.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.600
Or the more sinister belief
in fascist ideologies

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.480
that racial purity would
eliminate all evil from society.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.240
Perhaps this is why
much discussion of the topic

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.280
is now confined
to utopianism's dark side -

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.760
dystopianism,

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.920
a way of describing worlds,
real or imaginary,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.920
in entirely negative terms.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.560
From George Orwell's 1984 to
Margaret Atwood's A Handmaid's Tale,

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.280
dystopian fiction has become
increasingly popular in books,

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:57.840
films and television.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:01.520
But interest in utopias
isn't going anywhere -

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.720
references within books have been
on a steady rise since the 1900s

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.640
with clear spikes in the 60s
and also - perhaps surprisingly -

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.840
in the 80s.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:15.000
And who could deny the perfection of
the world - at least in microcosm -

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.680
as you sit by an ocean

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.040
and listen to the sound of the waves
crashing on a beach.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:23.800
Or when you first see a blanket
of bluebells in the spring.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.160
And without at least striving for
a better world, where would we be?

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.980
In chains,
with rats chewing off our faces,

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.200
that's where.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.880
